{"files":[{"content":"#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#ifdef _OPENMP\n#include <omp.h>\n#endif\n\ntypedef struct {\n    long int start;\n    long int total;\n    long int next;\n} bucket;\n\nstatic char *sort_strings;\nstatic int sort_length;\n\nstatic int compare_indices(const void *left, const void *right) {\n    long int a = *(const long int *)left;\n    long int b = *(const long int *)right;\n\n    return strcmp(sort_strings + a * sort_length,\n                  sort_strings + b * sort_length);\n}\n\nlong int *bucket_sort(char *a, int length, long int size, int offset,\n                      int nbuckets) {\n    long int *returns = malloc(sizeof(*returns) * (size > 0 ? size : 1));\n    bucket *buckets = calloc((size_t)nbuckets, sizeof(*buckets));\n    long int i;\n    long int prefix = 0;\n    int used_private_scatter = 0;\n\n#ifdef _OPENMP\n    /* Repeated bucket increments have loop-carried dependencies, so do not\n       mark these loops SIMD. Private histograms give each worker independent\n       counters while retaining a disjoint destination range per bucket. */\n    if (size > (long int)nbuckets * 64) {\n        int max_threads = omp_get_max_threads();\n        size_t cells = 0;\n        long int *local_counts = NULL;\n        long int *local_next = NULL;\n\n        if (max_threads > 1 && nbuckets > 0 &&\n            (size_t)max_threads <= (size_t)-1 / (size_t)nbuckets) {\n            cells = (size_t)max_threads * (size_t)nbuckets;\n            if (cells <= (size_t)-1 / sizeof(*local_counts)) {\n                local_counts = calloc(cells, sizeof(*local_counts));\n                local_next = malloc(cells * sizeof(*local_next));\n            }\n        }\n\n        if (local_counts != NULL && local_next != NULL) {\n#pragma omp parallel num_threads(max_threads)\n            {\n                int tid = omp_get_thread_num();\n                int team_size;\n                long int quotient;\n                long int remainder;\n                long int extra_before;\n                long int begin;\n                long int end;\n                long int j;\n                size_t row = (size_t)tid * (size_t)nbuckets;\n\n#pragma omp single\n                team_size = omp_get_num_threads();\n\n                quotient = size / team_size;\n                remainder = size % team_size;\n                extra_before = tid < remainder ? tid : remainder;\n                begin = (long int)tid * quotient + extra_before;\n                end = begin + quotient + (tid < remainder ? 1 : 0);\n\n                for (j = begin; j < end; j++) {\n                    int bucket_index = (unsigned char)a[j * length] - offset;\n                    local_counts[row + (size_t)bucket_index]++;\n                }\n\n#pragma omp barrier\n#pragma omp single\n                {\n                    prefix = 0;\n                    for (i = 0; i < nbuckets; i++) {\n                        int t;\n                        buckets[i].start = prefix;\n                        for (t = 0; t < team_size; t++) {\n                            size_t cell = (size_t)t * (size_t)nbuckets +\n                                          (size_t)i;\n                            local_next[cell] = prefix;\n                            prefix += local_counts[cell];\n                        }\n                        buckets[i].total = prefix - buckets[i].start;\n                    }\n                }\n\n                for (j = begin; j < end; j++) {\n                    int bucket_index = (unsigned char)a[j * length] - offset;\n                    size_t cell = row + (size_t)bucket_index;\n                    returns[local_next[cell]++] = j;\n                }\n            }\n            used_private_scatter = 1;\n        }\n\n        free(local_counts);\n        free(local_next);\n    }\n#endif\n\n    if (!used_private_scatter) {\n        for (i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n            int bucket_index = (unsigned char)a[i * length] - offset;\n            buckets[bucket_index].total++;\n        }\n\n        for (i = 0; i < nbuckets; i++) {\n            buckets[i].start = prefix;\n            buckets[i].next = prefix;\n            prefix += buckets[i].total;\n        }\n\n        for (i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n            int bucket_index = (unsigned char)a[i * length] - offset;\n            buckets[bucket_index].next++;\n            returns[buckets[bucket_index].next - 1] = i;\n        }\n    }\n\n    sort_strings = a;\n    sort_length = length;\n\n    /* Each bucket owns a disjoint index range; sorting is race-free. */\n#pragma omp parallel for schedule(dynamic, 1) if (size > (long int)nbuckets * 64)\n    for (i = 0; i < nbuckets; i++) {\n        qsort(returns + buckets[i].start, (size_t)buckets[i].total,\n              sizeof(*returns), compare_indices);\n    }\n\n    free(buckets);\n    return returns;\n}\n\nvoid load(char **vString, long int *N, int *l, int *os, int *nb) {\n    char *strings = NULL;\n    int len;\n    int offset;\n    int nbucket;\n    long int n;\n    long int i;\n\n    if (!fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &len)) {\n        printf(\"ERROR len\\n\");\n        exit(1);\n    }\n\n    if (!fscanf(stdin, \"%ld\", &n)) {\n        printf(\"ERROR n\\n\");\n        exit(1);\n    }\n\n    if (!fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &offset)) {\n        printf(\"ERROR offset\\n\");\n        exit(1);\n    }\n\n    if (!fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &nbucket)) {\n        printf(\"ERROR nbucket\\n\");\n        exit(1);\n    }\n\n    nbucket = nbucket + 1;\n    len = len + 1;\n\n    strings = (char *)malloc(n * len);\n\n    for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        if (!fscanf(stdin, \"%s\", strings + (i * len))) {\n            printf(\"ERROR %ld\\n\", i);\n            exit(1);\n        }\n    }\n\n    *vString = strings;\n    *N = n;\n    *l = len;\n    *os = offset;\n    *nb = nbucket;\n}\n\nvoid print(char *strings, long int *index, long int n, int len) {\n    long int i;\n\n    for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        printf(\"%ld -> %s\\n\", i, strings + (index[i] * len));\n    }\n}\n\nvoid save(char *strings, long int *index, long int n, int len) {\n    long int i;\n\n    for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        printf(\"%s\\n\", strings + (index[i] * len));\n    }\n}\n\nint main(int ac, char **av) {\n    char *strings = NULL;\n    long int N = 0;\n    long int *index = NULL;\n    int len = 0;\n    int offset;\n    int nbuckets;\n\n    load(&strings, &N, &len, &offset, &nbuckets);\n\n    index = bucket_sort(strings, len, N, offset, nbuckets);\n\n    save(strings, index, N, len);\n\n    if (strings != NULL)\n        free(strings);\n\n    if (index != NULL)\n        free(index);\n\n    return EXIT_SUCCESS;\n}\n","path":"src/bucketsort.c"}],"hypothesis":"The bucket-count and scatter passes have loop-carried dependencies because multiple elements may target the same bucket, so they cannot safely be marked SIMD. For sufficiently large inputs, per-thread histograms and cursors over disjoint input chunks can remove cross-thread conflicts while preserving exact bucket ranges; this may reduce serial preprocessing time before the existing parallel bucket sorts.","notes":"This is an unmeasured candidate. Small inputs and builds without OpenMP retain the serial count/scatter path; allocation failure also falls back to it. The controller should evaluate correctness and speed.","sources_kept":[],"transformations":["For large inputs in OpenMP builds, count bucket membership in per-thread histograms over balanced, disjoint input chunks.","Prefix-sum each bucket's per-thread counts to assign exclusive scatter ranges, then scatter each chunk using its private cursors.","Keep the existing serial path as a fallback and retain independent parallel sorting of disjoint bucket ranges."]}